Third-party components

The terms above apply to this project's own source code and assets only. This
software links against third-party open-source components, each of which
remains under its own license.

THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, distributed alongside this file and installed with the
application, is the authoritative inventory. It is generated from the lockfiles
by `scripts/gen-notices.mjs` and lists every component that is actually
compiled into the distributed binary, together with the license texts and
copyright notices those licenses require to be preserved on distribution.

Two entries there are worth calling out because they shape the distribution
terms above:

  - libgit2, the C library vendored by the libgit2-sys crate, is under
    GPL-2.0 WITH a linking exception. The exception grants "unlimited
    permission to link the compiled version of this library into combinations
    with other programs, and to distribute those combinations without any
    restriction" - that exception is what permits distributing this binary
    under the proprietary terms above. Note that the git2 and libgit2-sys
    crates declare MIT OR Apache-2.0 in their own manifests; that covers the
    Rust bindings, not the vendored C library.

  - tao is Apache-2.0 only, not the MIT OR Apache-2.0 dual license used by
    most of the surrounding Tauri crates.
